'''Yazoo''' is a bottled [[milk]]-based flavoured drink, produced by [[FrieslandCampina]] and sold in Belgium,<ref>[http://www.frieslandcampina.com/english/merken-en-producten/brands/yazoo.aspx Yazoo: milk. shaken up] {{Webarchive|url=https://web.archive.org/web/20140915025437/http://www.frieslandcampina.com/english/merken-en-producten/brands/yazoo.aspx |date=15 September 2014 }}, FrieslandCampina</ref> France, the United Kingdom and Ireland. Over eighty million bottles of Yazoo are sold annually.<ref name="yaz-prod" />

== Contents ==
Yazoo is available in four flavours; banana, chocolate, strawberry and vanilla.<ref name="yaz-prod">[http://www.yazoo.co.uk/our-products.html "Our Products"] {{Webarchive|url=https://web.archive.org/web/20111127094653/http://www.yazoo.co.uk/our-products.html |date=27 November 2011 }} from yazoo.co.uk</ref> Vanilla was introduced in 2014, as a limited edition flavour. It was announced that the Vanilla flavor and other flavours would be staying. Bottle sizes range from 200 ml, 400 ml, and one litre.

A new "No Added Sugar" range was introduced in 2016, in Strawberry, Banana and Toffee flavours.<ref>{{Cite web|url=https://www.talkingretail.com/products-news/chilled/yazoo-unveils-new-milk-drink-added-sugar-29-07-2016/|title=Yazoo unveils new milk drink with no added sugar|date=2016-07-29|website=Talking Retail|language=en-US|access-date=2019-07-17}}</ref> The following year, Chocolate was added to this range.<ref>{{Cite web|url=https://www.talkingretail.com/products-news/chilled/yazoo-adds-chocolate-flavour-no-added-sugar-range-24-10-2017/|title=Yazoo adds Chocolate flavour to No Added Sugar range|last=Cronin|first=Eilis|date=2017-10-24|website=Talking Retail|language=en-US|access-date=2019-07-17}}</ref> It was announced in November 2018 the range was to be rebranded as ''Yazoo Kids''.<ref>{{Cite web|url=https://www.talkingretail.com/products-news/chilled/yazoo-revamps-no-added-sugar-range-15-11-2018/|title=Yazoo revamps no added sugar range|last=Wells|first=Liz|date=2018-11-15|website=Talking Retail|language=en-US|access-date=2019-07-17}}</ref> 

In April 2018, a limited edition Choc Mint flavour was introduced (staying in the United Kingdom), following the results of a vote from consumers about the flavour they would most like to try as a milk drink. In April 2019, a limited edition Choc Caramel flavour was introduced replacing the Choc Mint flavour. FrieslandCampina said that Choc Mint had generated £1 million within five months of launch, and that the "target audience of sixteen to twenty four year olds are always looking for new flavours to try."{{cn|date=March 2025}}

The bottles of 2015 were designed by Steve Trotman. The smaller bottles usually have transparent straws glued to the side, in a plastic wrapper. The larger bottles feature a tearaway tag on the label for easy recycling.{{cn|date=March 2025}}

Yazoo is suitable for vegetarians; it is a source of [[calcium]], [[protein]], [[Vitamin B2|B<sub>2</sub>]] and [[Vitamin B12|B<sub>12</sub>]]. It is low in [[fat]] and contains no artificial sweeteners, colours or [[preservatives]].

== Advertising ==
Advertisements previously featured a green [[dinosaur]] mascot named ''Dino'', similar to [[Nesquik]]'s ''[[Quicky|Quicky the Rabbit]]''. The new line of bottles have the phrase, "Milk shaken up" on the label.{{cn|date=March 2025}}

