Stoney (drink):
{{Short description|African soft-drink beverage}}
{{More citations needed|date=December 2009}}
[[Image:Stoney tangawizi.jpg|thumb|Stoney Tangawizi, consumed in the Eastern [[Democratic Republic of the Congo]]]]
<!-- Image with unknown copyright status removed: [[Image:stoney.jpg]] -->
'''Stoney Ginger Beer''', or '''Stoney Tangawizi''' as it is called in [[Swahili language|Swahili]]-speaking [[Africa]], is a [[ginger beer]] soft-drink sold in several countries across the African continent. The product, sold in a brown bottle or can, is made and distributed by [[The Coca-Cola Company]].<ref>{{cite web|url= http://www.virtualvender.coca-cola.com/ft/index.jsp?brand_id=281|title= Product Descriptions|work= The Coca Cola Company|access-date= 23 February 2012|url-status= dead|archive-url= https://web.archive.org/web/20111007141546/http://www.virtualvender.coca-cola.com/ft/index.jsp?brand_id=281|archive-date= 7 October 2011}}</ref>

As is common with ginger beers in comparison to the lighter [[ginger ale]]s, the [[ginger]] flavour present in Stoney is especially intense. There are several varieties of Stoney in different parts of Africa. In South Africa there are three different stoneys, extra kwetsa, regular and sugar free and javaman kwetsa. Although they are all bottled by Coca-Cola, their recipes vary: the versions in Southern Africa tend to be more carbonated and sweeter, while the East Africa version tends to have a much stronger ginger taste. Stoney Ginger Beer was introduced in South Africa in 1971.<ref>{{cite web |url= http://www.cocacola.co.za/product_stoney.aspx|title= Stronger than the strongest thirst|work=Coca Cola South Africa|access-date=23 February 2012}}</ref>

